WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:04.934
How does an unpaid hospital bill physically harm a population's biology?

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.102
That mechanism is called financial toxicity.

3
00:00:08.618 --> 00:00:11.846
We usually treat medical debt as an isolated economic issue.

4
00:00:12.362 --> 00:00:16.038
Take a patient who receives an unexpected, unaffordable emergency room bill.

5
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.478
They aren't alone.

6
00:00:17.898 --> 00:00:21.574
41% of U.S. adults currently hold medical or dental debt.

7
00:00:21.962 --> 00:00:25.414
That's roughly 100 million people trapped by the cost of care.

8
00:00:25.962 --> 00:00:28.390
And this debt actively blocks future health care.

9
00:00:28.842 --> 00:00:33.190
64% of adults with medical debt skip needed treatment due to financial pressure.

10
00:00:33.706 --> 00:00:37.318
Getting treated for one illness becomes the direct barrier to treating the next.

11
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.718
This is financial toxicity at scale.

12
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:43.430
The 2024 JAMA study revealed a grim correlation.

13
00:00:43.946 --> 00:00:46.918
Counties with higher medical debt report more days of poor health,

14
00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.486
and higher mortality rates.

15
00:00:48.906 --> 00:00:51.910
The financial burden literally sickens and kills the community.

16
00:00:52.394 --> 00:00:55.302
But treating debt relief as public health infrastructure works.

17
00:00:55.594 --> 00:01:02.598
In 2025, Michigan automatically erased $144 million in medical debt for 210,000 residents.

18
00:01:02.954 --> 00:01:05.350
This functions as critical economic infrastructure.

19
00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:07.174
Not a residual charity cost.

20
00:01:07.594 --> 00:01:11.398
When the financial toxicity is cleared, the structural barrier to care vanishes with it.

21
00:01:11.882 --> 00:01:15.558
Because true prevention requires treating debt relief as public health infrastructure.

22
00:01:15.946 --> 00:01:16.870
Human in purpose.

23
00:01:17.098 --> 00:01:18.118
Systemic in method.

24
00:01:18.506 --> 00:01:19.558
Protective in outcome.
